ate": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 86941, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01B3kv4GLzSFBqvw9FKG2jQP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 90998, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QukiVBFDEDmhzJd6MHGX8j", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; the rollback was approved by a human reviewer. After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and work out why a release that was unhealthy in staging went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 129098, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QukiVBFDEDmhzJd6MHGX8j", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 129098, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QukiVBFDEDmhzJd6MHGX8j", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 133435, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.2.9 is older, and v2.3.1-rc only ever ran in staging. A human approver signed off on the rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Check after rollback:** All regions are on v2.3.0 and passing health checks. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It records the failing release, the rollback and approval, the health after the rollback, and the next steps.\n\nThe release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already failing health checks in staging, but v2.3.1 was still released to production. That's worth looking into along with the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JWZrcWr4YHJbsysAV6QCnt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019YBE6mNaQs15HHiSJAuv93", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SoEmY7xqcEkUPuFXrnPEBL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UozeM3jB7KooGr8cQ9nSvr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01B3kv4GLzSFBqvw9FKG2jQP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QukiVBFDEDmhzJd6MHGX8j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; the rollback was approved by a human reviewer. After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and work out why a release that was unhealthy in staging went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.2.9 is older, and v2.3.1-rc only ever ran in staging. A human approver signed off on the rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Check after rollback:** All regions are on v2.3.0 and passing health checks. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It records the failing release, the rollback and approval, the health after the rollback, and the next steps.\n\nThe release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already failing health checks in staging, but v2.3.1 was still released to production. That's worth looking into along with the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.", "type": "text"}]}]}